        'short' => 'This support helps you take part in cultural, religious or civic life, for example attending a place of worship, a community event or a local meeting, in ways that respect your beliefs and choices.',
        'overview' => "Belonging to a culture, faith or community is important to many people, and taking part in civic life gives a voice in decisions that affect you. For people with disability, practical barriers such as transport, physical access, communication or the need for personal support can get in the way of taking part.\n\nA support worker can help with the practicalities. That might mean going with you to a service at your place of worship, helping you attend a cultural festival, supporting you to enrol to vote or go to a council meeting, or helping you connect with a community group that matches your interests.\n\nThe support should reflect what matters to you, not what a provider assumes. Good providers ask about your beliefs and preferences, respect them, and where possible match you with workers who understand your culture, language or faith.",
