    'Customised prosthetics and orthotics' => [
        'cat' => 'Assistive technology & equipment',
        'short' => 'Prosthetics replace a missing limb or body part, and orthotics support or correct a part of the body. Customised devices are designed, made and fitted for one person by a qualified practitioner.',
        'overview' => "A prosthesis is an artificial limb or body part. An orthosis is a device such as a brace, splint or shoe insert that supports, protects or corrects a part of the body that is still there. Customised devices are made from measurements, scans or casts of the individual, so they fit properly and work with the way the person moves.\n\nProsthetists and orthotists are the health professionals who assess, design, fit and adjust these devices. They also teach people how to use and care for them. Because bodies change over time, and devices wear, regular reviews are an ongoing part of care rather than a one-off event.\n\nLook for practitioners with recognised qualifications and professional membership. Ask how many fittings are usually needed, how adjustments are handled and what support is available to help you learn to use a new device, especially in the early weeks.",
