        'overview' => "In a shared home, several people live together and receive support from a provider. The support might include help with personal care, meals, household tasks, medication and getting out into the community. Because people share staff, rosters and sometimes vehicles, the provider plans the day so that everyone gets the support they need.\n\nThe quality of a shared home depends heavily on how well people get on and how much say each person has. Good providers ask people about their preferences, involve them in decisions about the household and make sure people can choose how to spend their time, who visits and how their room is set up.\n\nShared living is one of several housing and support options. Others include living alone with support, living with family and specialist housing. It helps to compare the options and to ask questions about how the home is run, who else lives there and how staff are chosen and trained.",
